        {
          "type": "grid",
          "cards": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "Probe calibration",
              "heading_style": "title",
              "icon": "mdi:target-variant"
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text_only": true,
              "content": "Stored on the controller in flash and applied before anything is published, so Home Assistant, the panel and the device's own web page all get the corrected value. Survives reboots and OTA.\n\nThese are `entity_category: config`, which is why they were hard to find: Home Assistant files that category under the device page (Settings > Devices > Tank Monitor > Configuration) and leaves it out of auto-generated dashboards, so it never turns up where you would normally look. Pinned here so it is reachable."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "TDS — single point",
              "heading_style": "subtitle",
              "icon": "mdi:water-opacity"
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text_only": true,
              "content": "Bring the standard to **tank temperature** first — conductivity moves ~2%/°C, so a cold bottle bakes several percent of error into K permanently. Set the standard, stand the probe in it, wait for the reading to settle, then press Calibrate."
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "sensor.tank_monitor_tds",
              "name": "Reading now (raw)",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "number.tank_monitor_cal_tds_standard",
              "name": "Standard (ppm)",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              },
              "features": [
                {
                  "type": "numeric-input",
                  "style": "buttons"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "number.tank_monitor_cal_tds_k_factor",
              "name": "K factor",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              },
              "features": [
                {
                  "type": "numeric-input",
                  "style": "buttons"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "button.tank_monitor_calibrate_tds",
              "name": "Calibrate TDS",
              "icon": "mdi:target-variant",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              },
              "tap_action": {
                "action": "perform-action",
                "perform_action": "button.press",
                "target": {
                  "entity_id": "button.tank_monitor_calibrate_tds"
                },
                "confirmation": {
                  "text": "Recalibrate TDS so the probe reads the standard value right now? This overwrites the stored K factor."
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "Temperature",
              "heading_style": "subtitle",
              "icon": "mdi:thermometer-plus"
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text_only": true,
              "content": "Offset in °F against a reference thermometer. This probe is the only one the control loop has — if it reads low the heater will cook the tank while reporting the target, and nothing will notice."
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "sensor.tank_monitor_water_temperature",
              "name": "Reads now",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "number.tank_monitor_cal_temperature_offset",
              "name": "Offset (°F)",
              "grid_options": {
                "columns": 6
              },
              "features": [
                {
                  "type": "numeric-input",
                  "style": "buttons"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "pH — not in this firmware",
              "heading_style": "subtitle",
              "icon": "mdi:alert-outline"
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text_only": true,
              "content": "The running build has no pH sensor, no capture buttons and no slope — `packages/ph.yaml` is not compiled in. The **CO2 pH-floor cutoff automation is inert** for the same reason: it triggers on `sensor.tank_monitor_water_ph`, which does not exist, so CO2 currently has no automatic floor. The drop checker is the only backstop.\n\nCheck the C6 wrapper in the ESPHome dashboard for the `packages/ph.yaml` line."
            }
          ]
        }
